1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,553
Seventeenth of May, 2000. Forty thousand
people.

2
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:11,239
Extra time is over in the State Cup final,
and it all comes down to penalties.

3
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:15,846
Hapoel Tel Aviv against Beitar Jerusalem.

4
00:00:15,976 --> 00:00:18,949
Two each, after a hundred and twenty
minutes.

5
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:25,457
Two goals for Hapoel, one of them late in
normal time, the other deep into extra

6
00:00:25,497 --> 00:00:28,333
time. Now it comes down to the spot.

7
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:33,710
Four days earlier, these supporters had
seen the thing they had waited twelve

8
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:36,883
seasons for. Tonight, they want the rest
of it.

9
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:42,411
How did a club that had waited twelve
seasons end up here, one shoot-out from

10
00:00:42,451 --> 00:00:48,322
history? To find out, we have to go back
to the summer of

11
00:00:48,362 --> 00:00:48,901
1999.

12
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:56,885
The last league title had come in 1987/88.

13
00:00:57,015 --> 00:01:01,875
Since then, the red half of Tel Aviv had
watched the championship go elsewhere,

14
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,671
year after year.

15
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:07,912
Twelve seasons is a long time on a
terrace.

16
00:01:08,042 --> 00:01:13,911
Long enough for a child who stood there in
1988 to come back as a

17
00:01:13,951 --> 00:01:14,851
grown man.

18
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:18,216
There was one thing to hold on to.

19
00:01:18,346 --> 00:01:24,013
In 1998/99, Hapoel had won the State Cup.

20
00:01:24,143 --> 00:01:27,008
They started the new season as holders.

21
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:32,962
A cup is not a title. But it meant the new
season began with something to

22
00:01:33,002 --> 00:01:37,707
defend, and a reason to believe this group
could win the big games.

23
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,957
And there was a new man in charge.

24
00:01:41,087 --> 00:01:45,297
Dror Kashtan took over as manager on the
first of July,

25
00:01:45,577 --> 00:01:47,756
1999.

26
00:01:48,470 --> 00:01:51,818
Home was Bloomfield Stadium in Tel Aviv.

27
00:01:51,948 --> 00:01:55,010
Most of what follows starts and ends
there.

28
00:01:55,710 --> 00:02:00,267
The season would mean thirty-nine league
matches in a fourteen-team league, the

29
00:02:00,307 --> 00:02:03,315
State Cup, the Toto Cup, and Europe.

30
00:02:04,030 --> 00:02:08,050
Europe came first. And Europe would not be
kind.

31
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:16,008
Twelfth of August, 1999. The UEFA Cup
qualifying round,

32
00:02:16,248 --> 00:02:18,940
away to FC Yerevan in Armenia.

33
00:02:19,630 --> 00:02:23,505
A long journey north-east, for a club in a
hurry.

34
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:30,080
For supporters, a European night is a
different kind

35
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:33,727
of evening: a new country on the fixture
list, and the club's name read out

36
00:02:33,767 --> 00:02:34,652
somewhere it has never been heard.

37
00:02:35,350 --> 00:02:40,948
Hapoel won two-nil. Ronen Harazi scored
twice, two minutes apart,

38
00:02:41,128 --> 00:02:42,902
on fifty-eight and sixty.

39
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:48,497
Back home in the league, the opening night
brought a two-nil win over Hapoel

40
00:02:48,537 --> 00:02:53,950
Petah Tikva. Then a first stumble: a
two-one defeat at Bnei Yehuda.

41
00:02:54,630 --> 00:03:00,635
Remember Bnei Yehuda. They will matter
again at the very end of this story.

42
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:06,574
The second leg against Yerevan was won
two-one, with István Pisont scoring and

43
00:03:06,614 --> 00:03:10,892
Ygal Antebi adding another in the
ninetieth minute.

44
00:03:11,590 --> 00:03:16,610
Then Hapoel Kfar Saba came to Tel Aviv and
were beaten five-one,

45
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,725
Sebastian Simurotić scoring twice.

46
00:03:19,855 --> 00:03:23,245
The first real sign of what this team
could do.

47
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:28,942
In the first round proper, the draw sent
them to Scotland, to play Celtic.

48
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:32,221
Sixteenth of September, Glasgow.

49
00:03:32,351 --> 00:03:34,645
Celtic two, Hapoel nil.

50
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:39,361
Two weeks later, at home, Celtic won
again, one-nil.

51
00:03:39,491 --> 00:03:42,560
Europe was over by the end of September.

52
00:03:43,270 --> 00:03:47,627
The Toto Cup went the same way: out in the
round of sixteen, without scoring a

53
00:03:47,667 --> 00:03:52,447
goal against Maccabi Petah Tikva in either
leg.

54
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:57,427
Two competitions gone before the autumn
had really begun.

55
00:03:57,557 --> 00:04:01,934
What was left was the league, the cup they
were holding, and the old fear on the

56
00:04:01,974 --> 00:04:04,412
terraces: another lost year?

57
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:09,568
And in the league, something was starting
to happen.

58
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:13,109
A goalless draw with Maccabi Haifa.

59
00:04:13,239 --> 00:04:18,593
Then a win in Jerusalem, Kfir Udi scoring
just before half-time.

60
00:04:19,310 --> 00:04:22,524
Then four-nil against Maccabi Herzliya.

61
00:04:22,654 --> 00:04:25,966
Five-one away at Maccabi Petah Tikva.

62
00:04:26,096 --> 00:04:29,252
Three-nil against Maccabi Netanya.

63
00:04:29,382 --> 00:04:31,241
Two-one at Ashdod.

64
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:37,186
Four league games in October. Four wins,
fourteen goals scored.

65
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:43,837
Then the derby. Sixth of November, Hapoel
at home to Maccabi Tel Aviv.

66
00:04:44,550 --> 00:04:48,959
In a city split down the middle, nothing
else counts quite like this one.

67
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:52,605
Ronen Harazi scored in the eighth minute.

68
00:04:52,735 --> 00:04:54,431
It finished one each.

69
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:58,559
Harazi was becoming the name of the
season.

70
00:04:58,689 --> 00:05:03,964
He had already scored in Yerevan, at Bnei
Yehuda, and now in the derby.

71
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:08,884
Two weeks later, Beitar Jerusalem came and
lost four-one.

72
00:05:09,014 --> 00:05:13,773
The team that would meet them again in May
was learning that it could beat them.

73
00:05:14,470 --> 00:05:19,682
Three-one at Rishon LeZion. One-nil at
Hapoel Petah Tikva,

74
00:05:19,842 --> 00:05:23,950
Harazi again. A goalless draw at Hapoel
Haifa.

75
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:30,321
Then two one-nil wins in December, against
Bnei Yehuda and at Hapoel Kfar

76
00:05:30,361 --> 00:05:33,295
Saba. Not beautiful, but points.

77
00:05:33,990 --> 00:05:36,642
Most of the away trips were short ones.

78
00:05:36,772 --> 00:05:40,092
The whole league fitted inside a small
country.

79
00:05:40,790 --> 00:05:46,387
On Christmas Day, Hapoel went to Maccabi
Haifa, their closest challengers, and

80
00:05:46,427 --> 00:05:47,439
lost one-nil.

81
00:05:48,110 --> 00:05:53,555
It was only one defeat. But it came
against the club that would finish second.

82
00:05:53,685 --> 00:05:56,652
The race was on, and it was going to hurt.

83
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:03,755
The new year opened with a three-nil win
over Hapoel Jerusalem.

84
00:06:04,470 --> 00:06:10,354
On the first day of 2000, the goals came
from Ronen Harazi, Salim Toama and

85
00:06:10,394 --> 00:06:16,351
Ilan Bakhar. Three scorers, three goals,
and a team with more than one answer.

86
00:06:17,070 --> 00:06:22,684
A week later, away to Maccabi Herzliya,
Ronen Harazi scored three times in

87
00:06:22,724 --> 00:06:26,323
fifteen minutes. Hapoel won five-nil.

88
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:31,786
Then two more Harazi goals to beat Maccabi
Petah Tikva two-one.

89
00:06:31,916 --> 00:06:36,627
Five-two at Netanya. Four-two against
Ashdod.

90
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:41,610
Five games in January, five wins, nineteen
goals.

91
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:43,954
And then February.

92
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:49,525
Fifth of February: the return derby, away
to Maccabi Tel Aviv.

93
00:06:49,655 --> 00:06:51,802
Hapoel lost two-nil.

94
00:06:52,510 --> 00:06:56,372
A narrow win over Hapoel Haifa, Pisont
scoring.

95
00:06:56,502 --> 00:07:00,340
Then a two-nil defeat in Jerusalem, to
Beitar.

96
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:06,536
And on the twenty-sixth, at Bloomfield,
Ironi Rishon LeZion won two-one.

97
00:07:06,666 --> 00:07:10,484
Harazi's goal came in the eighty-sixth
minute, too late.

98
00:07:11,150 --> 00:07:13,857
Three defeats in four league games.

99
00:07:13,987 --> 00:07:18,512
The team that had scored nineteen in
January scored two in the whole of

100
00:07:18,552 --> 00:07:19,293
February.

101
00:07:19,990 --> 00:07:24,798
After twelve seasons of waiting, February
raised the old question on the

102
00:07:24,838 --> 00:07:28,195
terraces. Was it all about to go wrong
again?

103
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:35,042
The answer began three days later, in the
cup, at Maccabi Acre.

104
00:07:35,172 --> 00:07:37,369
Hapoel won two-one.

105
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:42,084
Then three-nil over Hapoel Jerusalem in
the league.

106
00:07:42,790 --> 00:07:46,948
Three days after that, the cup draw gave
the holders a derby.

107
00:07:47,078 --> 00:07:51,374
Hapoel against Maccabi Tel Aviv, seventh
of March.

108
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:55,067
Ilan Bakhar scored before half-time.

109
00:07:55,197 --> 00:08:00,524
Omri Afek made it two. Two-nil, and
Maccabi were out of the cup.

110
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:04,284
Omri Afek was becoming a name too.

111
00:08:04,414 --> 00:08:09,552
He had scored against Ashdod in January,
and he would score again at Hapoel

112
00:08:09,592 --> 00:08:12,816
Petah Tikva eleven days after the derby.

113
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:18,480
The league went on: one each with Maccabi
Haifa, three-nil at Hapoel Petah

114
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:21,078
Tikva, two-one over Beitar.

115
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:27,717
In the cup quarter-final at Hapoel Be'er
Sheva, Dean Računica and István

116
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:29,739
Pisont scored. Two-nil.

117
00:08:30,430 --> 00:08:34,060
The road to the final ran the length of
the country.

118
00:08:34,750 --> 00:08:40,192
There was still a stumble: a one-nil
defeat at Maccabi Petah Tikva on the first

119
00:08:40,232 --> 00:08:44,149
of April. Then three-one over Hapoel
Haifa.

120
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:47,841
Eleventh of April, the cup semi-final.

121
00:08:47,971 --> 00:08:53,831
Maccabi Haifa again, at home. No goals in
a hundred and twenty minutes.

122
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:57,249
Hapoel won the shoot-out two-one.

123
00:08:57,379 --> 00:08:59,653
The holders were in the final.

124
00:09:00,350 --> 00:09:05,386
Then a goalless draw at Ashdod, and the
league derby, twenty-second of April.

125
00:09:06,110 --> 00:09:10,751
Pisont scored at the end of the first
half, Salim Toama on the hour.

126
00:09:10,881 --> 00:09:16,523
Two-one to Hapoel. The derby that had been
lost in February was won in

127
00:09:16,563 --> 00:09:17,182
April.

128
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:20,576
Salim Toama's goal was the winner.

129
00:09:20,706 --> 00:09:25,535
For the supporters who had walked away
from the February derby in silence, this

130
00:09:25,575 --> 00:09:27,443
was the one that counted.

131
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:33,811
Two-one at Rishon LeZion. One-nil against
Hapoel Kfar Saba,

132
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:36,760
Pini Balili in the seventy-ninth minute.

133
00:09:36,890 --> 00:09:39,625
The title was close enough to touch.

134
00:09:39,755 --> 00:09:41,771
Now it had to be taken.

135
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:49,489
Thirteenth of May, 2000. Away to Bnei
Yehuda, the side that had

136
00:09:49,529 --> 00:09:52,308
beaten them on the second night of the
season.

137
00:09:52,990 --> 00:09:56,672
It finished one each. One each was enough.

138
00:09:56,802 --> 00:10:02,525
Hapoel Tel Aviv were champions of Israel,
with two league games still to play.

139
00:10:03,230 --> 00:10:08,692
The first league title since 1987/88.

140
00:10:08,822 --> 00:10:12,500
Twelve seasons of waiting, ended on one
afternoon.

141
00:10:13,190 --> 00:10:15,798
Four days later came the final.

142
00:10:15,928 --> 00:10:20,700
Hapoel and Beitar Jerusalem, in front of
forty thousand.

143
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:25,146
Dean Računica scored in the eighty-fifth
minute.

144
00:10:25,276 --> 00:10:29,915
Into extra time, and Salim Toama scored on
a hundred and fifteen.

145
00:10:30,045 --> 00:10:31,686
Two each at the end.

146
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:34,732
And so, back to where we started.

147
00:10:34,862 --> 00:10:38,638
Forty thousand people. Extra time over.

148
00:10:38,768 --> 00:10:39,925
Penalties.

149
00:10:40,590 --> 00:10:43,932
Hapoel Tel Aviv won the shoot-out
four-two.

150
00:10:44,062 --> 00:10:48,303
The State Cup stayed with Hapoel, and the
double was complete.

151
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:54,725
Five days in May. A title after twelve
seasons, and a cup kept.

152
00:10:54,855 --> 00:10:59,772
A week the red half of Tel Aviv would
carry for the rest of their lives.

153
00:11:00,470 --> 00:11:05,424
There was still the league to finish:
two-nil at home to Maccabi Herzliya, and

154
00:11:05,464 --> 00:11:08,310
one each at Netanya on the final day.

155
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:11,655
Pini Balili kept scoring to the end.

156
00:11:11,785 --> 00:11:17,332
At Rishon LeZion, against Kfar Saba, and
on the last day of the season at

157
00:11:17,372 --> 00:11:18,046
Netanya.

158
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:22,912
The final table: Hapoel Tel Aviv
eighty-five points.

159
00:11:23,042 --> 00:11:25,593
Maccabi Haifa seventy-six.

160
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:32,019
Thirty-nine league matches. Twenty-six
wins, seven draws, six defeats.

161
00:11:32,149 --> 00:11:35,280
Seventy-six goals for, twenty-eight
against.

162
00:11:35,990 --> 00:11:40,763
Those numbers come from the archive, match
by match, and they agree with the

163
00:11:40,803 --> 00:11:46,240
published table. Eighty-five points is
exactly what those results add up to.

164
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:52,096
A season that lost in Europe, went out of
one cup early, and wobbled badly in

165
00:11:52,136 --> 00:11:55,455
February. And still ended with the double.

166
00:11:56,150 --> 00:12:00,344
For the people who stood at Bloomfield
through those twelve seasons, it was

167
00:12:00,384 --> 00:12:02,629
never just a story about a team.

168
00:12:02,759 --> 00:12:08,553
It was a story about waiting. And about
being there, together, when the waiting

169
00:12:08,593 --> 00:12:08,925
ended.

170
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:15,188
Every match in this film is waiting in the
FanLife archive, with the games, the

171
00:12:15,228 --> 00:12:17,917
trivia and the stories of the whole club.

172
00:12:18,047 --> 00:12:22,151
Come and play it at fanlife.dubelteam.com.
